  "domain": "ai",
  "definition": "Real-time AI inference is the execution of trained machine learning model forward passes within latency bounds tight enough to support interactive or time-critical applications, typically measured in milliseconds to tens of milliseconds. It requires co-optimisation of model architecture, runtime software, and hardware accelerators \u2014 including GPUs, NPUs, and dedicated AI ASICs \u2014 to meet throughput and latency targets whilst maintaining acceptable accuracy. Applications include autonomous vehicles, real-time video analysis, voice assistants, and spatial computing overlays.",
